patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108831.patch","merged_at":"2025-07-22T16:27:17Z"},"body":"If you ran `JSON.stringify` on a single float, the `p_full_precision` option worked. However, this argument was not passed into the recursive calls, so if you tried to stringify an Array or Dictionary with floats in it, this option was broken.\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes that problem, and removes the default argument from the internal function to prevent this problem happening in the future. The public version of the function still has a default argument for `p_full_precision`. I also threw in making a few variables `const` while I was at it.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108831/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108831/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}